{
  "assembly_notes": "Reclining convertible sofa. One rigid sofa_frame root carries the carcass, the fixed arms, the seat decks and every hinge bracket. Each of seat_count seat units contributes a seat_back that is a REVOLUTE (+x) child of the frame reclining rearward into free space, and a legrest that is a REVOLUTE (+x) child of the frame hanging stowed in front of the plinth and swinging UP and forward to seat level. Both are independent joints and both sweep only into free space, so every single-joint boundary pose is clear. A recline_control knob is a REVOLUTE (+y) child of the frame on the outer arm. Four component slots vary without touching the mechanism: back_build, base_style, deck_build and legrest_style. seat_width_m, seat_depth_m and seat_height_m are independent continuous parameters deriving carcass width and depth, seat pitch, hinge stations and legrest length; palette is non-core.",
